					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-07-31 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>What&#39;s good, Mass Line fam? For those that don&#39;t know, I&#39;m Budo, a local beat maker, technology nerd, and gadget freak. It&#39;s a scary combo. In the coming days, weeks, and months I&#39;m going to be bringing you the latest and greatest from the world of technology and gadgetry. We&#39;ll explore the technical side of some of the hottest new studio equipment, bring reviews of the mobile technology you need to stay on top of game, and interview some of your favorite artists about their shameful secret lives as Sidekick-addicted, Macbook-loving nerds. We&#39;re gonna bring out the inner-geek in all of you. Trust me, it will be hot! For the time being, I&#39;ll hit you with some shots of the upcoming Sidekick Zante, aka the Sidekick Slide, courtesy of the Boy Genius Report. Stay tuned fam, and my gracious thanks to Mass Line for the oh-so-dope look!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-07-31 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>Now that the Block Party is over, it&#39;s time to start looking towards Bumbershoot for the next dose of hip hop at a Seattle festival. Bumbershoot 2007 has a great lineup, and they didn&#39;t skimp on the hip hop.<br /><br />The big show of course is Monday in the stadium with Wu-Tang and Lupe Fiasco. People always wonder who will actually perform at a Wu show. According to Bumbershoot booker Chris Porter, they have a contract with the following to show - RZA, GZA, Method Man, Raekwon, Ghostface Killah, Inspectah Deck, U-God, and Masta Killa. Should be a great show.<br /><br />Beyond that, other acts confirmed are K&#39;naan, Gabriel Teodros,&nbsp; D Black, Dyme Def, Step Cousins, The Saturday Knights, Ohmega Watts and Lyrics Born.<br /><br />check out the full linup at www.bumbershoot.org/lineup.htm<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-07-26 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Back from a week in <strong>Occupied Mexico</strong> (aka California) rocking shows in <strong>San Francisco</strong> and <strong>Los Angeles</strong>. Cali is brewing with more and more love for Blue Scholars and Massline each time we make the trip down I-5 South. But it&#39;s good to be back home for the weekend to rock the <strong>Capitol Hill Block Party</strong> (Friday, 8pm) with <strong>Sabzi</strong>, then hit the Vera Project stage to rock a set with <strong>Good Medicine</strong>! Then, <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> rocks the Neumo&#39;s stage on Saturday.<br /><br />Here&#39;s something that doesn&#39;t happen too often in a music publication: <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=272423">I got a chance to speak directly about political views in this week&#39;s <strong>The Stranger</strong> (look at the masterful illustration).</a> Nice. Even nicer, this year&#39;s Block Party lineup has the biggest look for hip-hop (especially local) in minute. Even nicer than that, you can catch ALL these performances without missing another. Look:<br /><br /><strong>Fri, Jul 28</strong><br />4:00pm - The Saturday Knights - Main Stage<br />5:45pm - Grynch - Vera Stage<br />7:15pm - D. Black - Vera Stage<br />8:00pm - Blue Scholars - Main Stage<br />9:45pm - Good Medicine - Main Stage<br />10:15pm - Cancer Rising - Neumo&#39;s Stage (21+)<br /><br /><strong>Sat, Jul 29</strong><br />6:45pm - Aesop Rock - Main Stage<br />5:30pm - Gabriel Teodros - Neumo&#39;s Stage (21+)<br />9:00pm - Dyme Def - Vera Stage<br /><br />I also recently penned an ode to the Northwest summer with the homie <a href="http://www.myspace.com/grynchmusic" title="Grynch"><strong>Grynch</strong>, which you can peep at his myspace page</a>!<br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-07-25 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://a342.ac-images.myspacecdn.com/images01/116/l_f260bf893a6e66ba1258339c34b67cb5.jpg" onmouseover="undefined" onmouseout="undefined" alt="" title="undefined" width="451" height="658" /><div>Say Hello / Goodbye to our friend and funnyman, Hari Kondabolu as he attempts to take over all of London. And if you slept and missed it, Hari was interviewed in today&#39;s Seattle Times. <a href="http://seattletimes.nwsource.com/html/entertainment/2003802720_comic24.html">Read it, foo! </a>&nbsp;Massline / Hari&#39;s short film &quot;Manoj&quot; will also be shown (directed by Sabzi&#39;s brother, Zia Mohajerjasbi).</div><div><br /></div><div>Did you buy your tickets for the Capitol Hill Block Party yet? Did you know there&#39;s gonna be a rare performance by Good Medicine after the Blue Scholars set? Hurry up and buy those tickets now, foo!</div><div><br /></div><div>peace</div><div>daps</div><div><br /></div><div><br /></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-07-21 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>SOMA rec center!&nbsp; we&#39;ll be there at 3pm folks!<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> [25] <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
